id: pm-vcs-provenance-catalog-scale
title: Measure and compact native provenance catalogs without weakening recovery
description: "Follow-up to PR 150 native erasure provenance. The correctness repair records one identity-only payload ownership file per object/FileId edge and rewrites the current native-output registry when publishing a working file. Measure complete data-plus-control byte, inode and write costs across growing histories and materialized working sets. Evaluate a compact catalog or batch publication only with equivalent durable source attribution before bytes, strict native ownership classification, backward-readable schemas and every crash/recovery guard retained. Existing object-root pack measurements do not establish total clone metadata or checkout scaling."
type: Task
status: open
priority: 3
tags[3]: follow-up,performance,provenance
created_at: "2026-11-01T02:12:37.718Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-01T02:12:57.169Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "Publish data-plus-control byte and inode counts and write/read costs for increasing FileId histories; preserve native source closure, refusal schemas, publication ordering and crash convergence; keep existing coverage thresholds and backward reads; make no performance claim before measurement."
